{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-92078",
  "enisaUuid": "9e4b0dea-555d-3805-8f32-c545935e192c",
  "description": "A flaw has been found in Ahsay AhsayCBS up to 9.15.2.69/10.3.4.44. This vulnerability affects unknown code of the file /rps/api/json/UpdateReceivers.do of the component Replication Receiver. Executing a manipulation of the argument random can lead to os command injection. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit has been published and may be used. Upgrading to version 9.15.2.70 and 10.3.4.45 is able to resolve this issue. Upgrading the affected component is advised. The initial patch did not fix the security vulnerability properly. An update of the CVE entry to reflect this became necessary.",
  "datePublished": "Oct 4, 2026, 5:30:12 AM",
  "dateUpdated": "Oct 26, 2026, 2:31:13 PM",
  "baseScore": 10.0,
